"nine_ball_help_differences" = "Differences";
"nine_ball_help_event_defense" = "Legal safeties are allowed and do not score separately. There is no casual handoff action. A third-foul loss gives the rack to the opponent.";
"nine_ball_help_event_fouls" = "For each player, count fouls within the same rack, not necessarily consecutively. The first two give the opponent %1$d each. The third gives %2$d and loses the rack. Do not add another foul or normal-win award. Three fouls therefore award %3$d in total. Clear both counts at the next rack.";
"nine_ball_help_event_nine" = "A legal 9 on the break scores small gold. There is no separate golden-9 category. If the break also contains a foul, spot the 9 and apply the foul; the opponent has ball in hand.";
"nine_ball_help_event_racks" = "Play %d total racks, not a race to that many wins. Higher points win; ties continue into extra racks. After a rack, finish early only if the trailing player cannot tie even using the remaining racks’ maximum points, including foul awards and custom values.";
"nine_ball_help_event_wins" = "Big gold (%1$d): the breaker runs out. Small gold (%2$d): includes a legal 9 on the break, all nine object balls pocketed on the break, or a continuous break-and-combination into the 9 after potting on the break. Away from the break, a runout from a table still containing the 1 and 9 qualifies; a combination during that runout does not. Other legal wins score %3$d.";
"nine_ball_help_folk_break_next" = "After any winning result, the next seat after the winner breaks.";
"nine_ball_help_folk_break_retain" = "After a normal win or small gold, the next seat after the winner breaks. After big gold or golden 9, the winner breaks again.";
"nine_ball_help_folk_fouls" = "A foul transfers %d from the offender to the next seat, who receives ball in hand. No extra ball-in-hand points. A handoff selects another player to continue without scoring or ending the rack. This casual preset does not track three-foul losses.";
"nine_ball_help_folk_intro" = "Points transfer between players: the winner gains what the others pay. 14710 and 1357 use the same casual rules in this app, with different point values.";
"nine_ball_help_folk_wins" = "Big gold: the breaker clears the rack; every opponent pays %1$d. Small gold: a qualifying clearance after taking over; the payer pays %2$d. Normal win: one payer pays %3$d, initially the winner’s previous seat. Players confirm the actual payer.";
"nine_ball_help_fouls_handoff" = "Fouls & handoff";
"nine_ball_help_golden" = "A legal 9 on the break or a legal combination into the 9 is a separate golden-9 result in this preset. Each opponent pays %d. Its value is configured separately from the four scheme numbers.";
